# The documented key list for the Docker Compose deployment (slice-01 step 7).
#
# `aspire publish` / `aspire deploy` write the real files beside the generated compose file,
# in the git-ignored output directory (aspire-output/):
#
#   .env              written KEYS-ONLY by publish, and it PRESERVES any value already
#                     present on a later publish. Values typed in by hand persist; generated
#                     secrets never land here.
#   .env.Production   written by DEPLOY with RESOLVED VALUES, rebuilt each run. This is the
#                     file that carries the generated database password.
#
# NEVER commit either. This file lives in deploy/ because the output directory is ignored
# as a directory - anything placed there is un-committed by the rule that protects them.
#
# These are the keys the generated compose file reads (Aspire 13.5.4):

# Container image for the Api (the web app is built into it, served from wwwroot).
API_IMAGE=
# The Api's port inside the container. The compose file publishes it on 127.0.0.1 only.
API_PORT=
# Container image for the one-shot Migrator.
MIGRATOR_IMAGE=
# Generated per deployment. Never reuse one, never commit one.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
